ggers activate she throws  out a bomb depending on whether you're  holding back forward or nothing is  explode at different times the V trigger  bar will then start depleting and she  has a limited window to throw a second  bomb these comically large bombs are  incredibly disruptive and it's difficult  to tell exactly when they'll explode  which makes them great for relieving  pressure naturally they also help  themselves for example if you keys c'mon  - can be used to quickly travel across  the screen and through an opponent on to  the other side this puts him in a spot  where they have to deal with an  explosion and possibly an overhead or a  grab  of course bombs can also be used to  extend combos for example and one of her  many target combos by activating V  trigger to throw the bomb out then use a  light punch and cancel into a excu nice  push them into the bomb which will then  send them flying into the air where  every key can follow up with even more  attacks ourselves bombs can also be  triggered early by throwing an explosive  kunai at them  and the positioning can be moved around  by a tack room directly with punches or  kicks v-trigger bombs will no doubt  become a core part of maximizing Ibuki  damage Airport is also a fantastic way  of dissuading players from rushing  relieving pressure and generally  upsetting the flow of the match other  tools in a bookies arsenal include herby  skill which functions much like Karin's  palm strike and cancels out projectiles  it can also be charged so that when it's  blocked it remains relatively safe she  can also come and grab during which he  summons an energy ball much like  Naruto's Rasengan and plunges it into  her opponent launching them across the  screen this is handy to back the  opponent to a corner or knock them down  for more setups in terms of mobility the  booty has quite a fast walk speed but  you can also leap into the air and use a  parachute to glide for a short distance  this is great for escaping corners or  needs to be well timed since players can  chase her down and capture  on her vulnerability while she's falling  Ibuki can cover for this somewhat by  throwing a single kunai largely she has  a shot you can like kicks but unlike the  show you cans there's no invincibility  on these if it hits the e X version can  be canceled at the very top of its arc  into a kunai or an exp knife or a juggle  overall Ibuki feels like she's going to  emerge as one of the stronger characters  in the three-point-five roster and many  specials and target combos are great for  controlling space and dishing out big  damage the sheer number of abilities she  has makes her great for overwhelming at  home but to balance this out she has  very low health she feels very much like  a glass cannon for morals free fire 5  including videos on the game's upcoming  story mode keep an eye on GameSpot's  youtube page and don't forget to  subscribe  devour  you
 

